 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the local finance law, in relation to authorizing the village\nof Hempstead, county of Nassau, to amortize the cost of payments to employees\nupon separation of service from the village",
    "basePrintNo": "S10489",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10489-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11.00, Loc Fin L",
    "lawSection": "Local Finance Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10489\n\nSPONSOR: BYNOE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the local finance law, in relation to authorizing the\nvillage of Hempstead, county of Nassau, to amortize the cost of payments\nto employees upon separation of service from the village\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the Village of Hempstead to finance over time certain costs\nassociated with employee separations, including early retirement incen-\ntives and accrued leave payouts.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends paragraph a of section 11.00 of the local\nfinance law by adding a new subdivision 111 to authorize the Village of\nHempstead to treat specified separation payments as a capital expense.\n\nThe bill applies to payments made on or after April 1, 2026, including\nbut not limited t; separation incentives; payments for accrued and\nunused leave time; compensation in lieu of overtime; and other required\nseparation-related payments. Such expenditures may be financed with a\nmaximum period of probable usefulness of twenty years.\n\nSection 2 provides that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCurrent law generally requires these costs to be paid in the year\nincurred, which can create significant fiscal pressure on local budgets.\nThis bill authorizes the Village to amortize such costs over time,\nallowing for more stable budget planning and better alignment between\nupfront expenditures and long-term savings derived from personnel cost\nreductions. Providing this financing flexibility will assist the Village\nin responsibly managing its fiscal affairs while pursuing cost-saving\nworkforce strategies.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nThis bill has no fiscal impact on the State. It is expected to have a\npositive fiscal management impact for the Village of Hempstead by allow-\ning certain expenditures to be financed over time.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
